function P = phase5b_pickup(device, Iload_A, Imin_fault_A)
%PHASE5B_PICKUP  Pickup-setting engine v2: Siemens DT baseline + study rules (Phase-5b Tasks C3/C4).
%   P = PHASE5B_PICKUP(device, Iload_A, Imin_fault_A) returns struct P with
%   v1 fields (setting/unit/basis/source/validation/device_id/
%   assumption_class) plus study tags (tms/curve/use_phase5_time/
%   setting_sec_A; EF rows also carry ef_tms) for STUDY devices, or tdef/
%   time_status/curve/use_phase5_time/setting_sec_A for the PHYSICAL
%   baseline device GEN-51-SIEMENS-BL.
%
%   Inputs mirror phase5_pickup (frozen v1, never modified):
%     device       registry row scalar struct (must carry non-empty char
%                  device_id; baseline branch dispatches on
%                  'GEN-51-SIEMENS-BL').
%     Iload_A      normal-load anchor in PRIMARY A (scalar, finite, >= 0).
%     Imin_fault_A minimum fault current in PRIMARY A (scalar, finite, > 0).
%
%   Baseline branch (spec S3/S5; ledger SIEMENS-Igt-1.14A +
%   SIEMENS-tdef-3s-??, class USER_ASSERTED_PENDING_DOC):
%     7UM622 50/51 I> ON, inverse disabled, I> = 1.14 A secondary
%     ~= 17171 A primary via generator T1/T2 15000/1 CTs (SOURCE-BACKED,
%     unchanged), tdef = 3.00 s marked ??/coordination-pending so operating
%     time stays NOT-DETERMINABLE-??-PENDING-COORDINATION until coordination
%     info arrives. DERIVED cross-check recorded (not substituted):
%     1.20 x Imax 14309 A = 17170.8 A ~= 17171 A; 17171/15000 = 1.1447 A
%     ~= 1.14 A secondary. Inverse (phase5_time/phase5_curve) is prohibited
%     on this row by contract: P.curve = 'DT-??' (refused by the locked v1
%     library: only exact 'DT' enters the definite-time path) and
%     P.use_phase5_time = false (downstream callers must check the flag and
