function R = run_phase5b_production(tag, varargin)
%RUN_PHASE5B_PRODUCTION  End-to-end Phase-5b production-v2 driver (Task C11).
%   R = RUN_PHASE5B_PRODUCTION(tag) builds every Phase-5b protection output
%   from the frozen Phase-4 production archive (read-only) and writes
%   results/phase5_protection_v2/ via PHASE5B_WRITER:
%     10 CSVs (device_registry, relay_settings, fault_inputs,
%     relay_currents, coordination_matrix, coordination_margins,
%     breaker_duty, sensitivity, validation, NEW phase5b_effectiveness)
%     + manifest.json + run_log.txt + sha256.txt, plus TCC plots via
%     PHASE5B_TCC into plots/ (regenerated deterministically; hashes
%     recorded; the C10 plots are overwritten in place inside the v2 dir
%     only — either choice is allowed if documented, and regeneration is
%     the choice recorded here).
%
%   R = RUN_PHASE5B_PRODUCTION(tag, 'overwrite', true) re-runs into the
%   existing results/phase5_protection_v2 directory. Without the flag, an
%   existing directory errors error('phase5b_production:exists').
%   Default tag 'production-v2' (manifest tag only; the output directory is
%   fixed results/phase5_protection_v2; results/phase5_protection stays
%   frozen untouched).
%
%   LOCKED RECOMPUTE CHAIN (ledger ruling — implemented exactly, read ALL
%   consumers first, modified nothing):
%   (a) phase5_import T40 (frozen v1, read-only; 40-row backbone).
%   (b) phase5b_registry v2 devices (C2 study rows + C7 physical rows).
%   (c) Study pickups resolved via phase5b_pickup C4 rules (GEN 17170.8 =
%       1.20x14309 Imax; GSUT 1380 = 1.2xmax(1150, 870.7726); GIS 1.2xFL
%       LINE_Q9 formula via 1600/1; EF 5 A retained sensitive case; EF TMS
%       0.15 from PICKUP, never registry 0.20) and injected (resolved
%       pickup/TMS/curve) into a devices copy — the registry itself is
%       never edited. Siemens-baseline rows (GEN-51-SIEMENS-BL, DT-??) are
%       NEVER dispatched to phase5_time: the DT-?? path is excluded from
%       time/margin computation with a ?? reason (use_phase5_time false is
%       asserted, and no phase5_time call ever sees a DT-?? curve).
%   (d) Relay currents via phase5_ct arithmetic with v2 CTs (15000 gen /
%       1600 GSUT-GIS): branch primaries from the coord matrix sides
%       (I_primary = I_secondary x CT_device). The frozen phase5_ct_table
%       wrapper rejects 1600 by its locked ratio guard (15000/16000 only),
%       and frozen files are never modified, so conversion calls phase5_ct
%       directly — the single source of truth phase5_ct_table delegates to
%       (concern C11-REL-CT in the task report).
%   (e) Operating times via frozen phase5_time (TMS 0.20 study phase,
%       0.15 EF) inside frozen phase5_coord.
%   (f) Coordination via frozen phase5_coord on the v2-resolved devices.
%   (g) Duty via phase5b_duty wrapper (52G 100 kA SOURCE-BACKED +
%       equipment/interrupting column split).
%   (h) Sensitivity: BLOCKED on frozen phase5_sensitivity reuse (evidence:
%       phase5_sensitivity.m:137 'IsUp = pkUp / 2000', :190 'primUp / 2000',
%       :193 reason 'upstream-GSUT-HV-51-2000/1-untouched', comments :9/:11
%       '2000/1 STUDY CTs' — v1 CT hard-coded on the upstream leg instead of
%       reading device ct_ratio, which is 1600 in v2; pinned by
%       test_phase5b_writer). The frozen file is NOT modified; the
%       v2-adapted GEN-scope sensitivity is computed in the local
%       SENSITIVITY_V2 engine below (reads device pickups/CTs, 1600 upstream
%       dial, EF TMS 0.15; frozen phase5_ct/phase5_time only).
%   (i) Effectiveness via phase5b_effectiveness (single branch-phasor call,
%       ~5 min, reused across all rows inside the module; F4 uses B1/B2
%       section rows, never the LINE_total cancellation residual).
%   (j) phase5b_writer writes all v2 CSVs + effectiveness table + manifest
%       (input SHA = v1 production SHA + v1-outputs reference; code hashes
%       incl. phase5b_* + v1 modules used) + sha256 + run_log under
%       results/phase5_protection_v2/ (tag production-v2).
%
%   Validation/tests: live phase5_validate() supplies the validation CSV
%   and manifest reference (frozen framework regression; v2 legs B01+ arrive
%   in C12 phase5b_validate); run_phase5_tests() runs after the tables and
%   TCC plots but BEFORE phase5b_writer, so NP/NF land in run_log.txt
%   before sha256.txt is hashed (never appended after hashing). Counts
